      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 947: 🟡 **Repeated same-tip offers can get permanently ignored after two transient failures.** `onRepositoryMessage()` drops `have` when it equals `link.wanted`, and `repositoryFetchDone()` only retries once (`retried`). After the second failure, `wanted` stays at that tip, so later re-offers of the same tip won’t trigger another fetch. This can leave peers stuck until a newer tip appears. Consider clearing `wanted/requested` (or allowing same-tip reattempts with backoff) when terminal failure is reached.",
